window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-2bd4c847a4cfb895"]={"key":"ny_b1-2bd4c847a4cfb895","group":"ny_b1","uid":"2bd4c847a4cfb895","rank":41,"title":"clearwater application findings narrative","occupation":"real_estate_sales_agents","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are Iris Macaulay, the senior real estate sales agent at Clearwater Housing Trust, which manages leasing for Latchford Media’s 44-unit building. Isabel Lindqvist has complained to Xiomara Sheridan, Latchford’s owner representative, that her completed rental application was never sent to the owner and that a later applicant received the unit. Xiomara needs a reliable account before answering her tomorrow. The available record is limited to these facts: Clearwater held open houses on April 6 and April 13; an undated sign-in sheet includes Isabel’s handwritten name but cannot be tied to either session; the portal records her application as created on April 8 at 10:14 a.m. and saved, but never submitted, with no timestamp showing staff receipt of a completed application; and a partial text export shows Isabel asking Mariam Braithwaite at 11:02 a.m. on April 8, “did that go through?”, Mariam replying at 11:19 a.m., “I can only see drafts until you hit submit,” and Isabel writing at 9:07 a.m. on April 12, “I sent everything earlier this week.” The export skips the intervening four days and is not certified complete. Mariam remembers calls on April 9 and April 11 in which she says she repeated that the application remained a draft, but there are no call notes or recordings. The later applicant submitted at 8:42 a.m. on April 12, was screened that day, and was accepted at 3:30 p.m. on April 13; we have no comparative qualification information. The team often uses the earliest portal timestamp to describe application order, although this portal separately labels created, saved, and submitted events. Eamon Kilgore handles fair-housing and legal determinations, but Xiomara needs the operational record first. Prepare `application_findings.docx` as a neutral findings narrative for Xiomara, followed by a numbered evidence index. Keep every factual statement traceable to an index entry, make clear what the record does and does not establish, and do not invent missing messages, portal activity, qualifications, motives, or legal conclusions. Keep the complete document to no more than three pages. Write the file into the top level of the working directory using exactly that filename.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `application_findings.docx` — Owner-facing findings narrative concerning the disputed application sequence, followed by a numbered evidence index. (Use exactly the filename application_findings.docx.; Place the file at the top level of the working directory.; Limit the complete document to three pages.; Include a neutral findings narrative and a numbered evidence index.; Make factual statements traceable to the evidence index.; Do not invent missing evidence, comparative qualifications, motives, or legal conclusions.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/application_findings.docx","bytes":40524,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/f700f4b3a47ddd465dcb98156958cabbc4ecaccdbe98e756bc33d0313e001c51.docx","sha256":"f700f4b3a47ddd465dcb98156958cabbc4ecaccdbe98e756bc33d0313e001c51","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Application Findings Narrative\nTo: Xiomara Sheridan, Owner Representative, Latchford Media    From: Iris Macaulay, Senior Real Estate Sales Agent, Clearwater Housing Trust    Date: 20 April\nBottom line. This is an operational reconstruction of the limited record for the April 6-13 review period. The portal shows Isabel Lindqvist's application was created and saved on April 8, but it contains no recorded submission event or timestamp showing staff receipt of a completed application [2]. That finding does not verify Isabel's statement that she sent everything, and it does not establish that Clearwater received and failed to forward a completed application. The retained texts, an undated sign-in sheet, and an unrecorded call recollection leave material gaps, so the record is not a basis for categorical exoneration or for a legal conclusion [1][3][4].\nIssue presented\nIsabel's complaint contains two separate propositions: (1) that a completed application was not transmitted to the owner, and (2) that a later applicant received the unit. The operational record can test timing and handling evidence; it cannot, on this record, decide motive, comparative qualifications, discrimination, or liability.\nChronology and findings\nClearwater held open houses on April 6 and April 13 [1]. An undated sign-in sheet includes Isabel's handwritten name, but it cannot be tied to either session. It supports possible open-house contact only; it does not establish attendance on a particular date, application completion, submission, or priority [1].\nOn April 8 at 10:14 a.m., the portal records Isabel's application as created and saved, with no submitted status and no portal timestamp showing staff receipt of a completed application [2]. Created, saved, and submitted are different portal events: creation starts a record, saving preserves draft work, and submission is the milestone that would show the application was sent through this portal. The available record therefore supports creation and saving, not a recorded submission. The absence of a portal event is not proof that transmission through every possible channel was impossible [2].\nThe partial text export records Isabel asking Mariam Braithwaite at 11:02 a.m. on April 8, \"did that go through?\" Mariam replied at 11:19 a.m., \"I can only see drafts until you hit submit.\" Isabel later wrote at 9:07 a.m. on April 12, \"I sent everything earlier this week\" [3]. These messages are evidence of what the parties wrote at those times, not proof that the export captures the whole conversation. The four-day gap between the retained April 8 and April 12 messages is material, and the export is not certified complete [3].\nMariam recalls calls on April 9 and April 11 in which she says she repeated that the application remained a draft [4]. That recollection is relevant but less independently verifiable than a contemporaneous timestamped record because there are no call notes or recordings [4]. The record cannot determine whether any unrecorded communication, attachment, or alternate delivery occurred during the gap.\nThe later applicant's portal record shows submission at 8:42 a.m. on April 12, screening on April 12, and acceptance at 3:30 p.m. on April 13 [5]. April 12 is the material change point: the later applicant has a recorded submission before Isabel's retained 9:07 a.m. statement that she had sent everything earlier that week [3][5]. That sequence does not, by itself, show displacement, causation, or a preference for the later applicant. Comparative qualification information is unavailable, so no ranking of the applicants is supportable [5].\nApplication order and boundaries\nThe team's practice of using the earliest portal timestamp to describe order is reliable only when the timestamps represent comparable milestones. Isabel's April 8 timestamp is creation; the later applicant's April 12 timestamp is submission. They are not like-for-like events, so Isabel's earlier creation time does not establish submission priority [2][5].\nAccordingly, Xiomara can safely describe the principal record finding as: Isabel's portal record shows creation and saving but no recorded submission by Isabel, while the later applicant has a recorded submission and later acceptance [2][5]. She should describe Isabel's transmission assertion and any staff failure to forward a completed application as unverified, not as established fact [2][3][4]. The record also does not establish discriminatory selection, disparate treatment, improper preference, or any protected-class fact; those are outside this operational account. Eamon Kilgore is the appropriate person for fair-housing and legal determinations.\nNumbered Evidence Index\n1. Open-house sign-in record (Clearwater leasing file; sessions April 6 and April 13; sheet itself undated). Open houses occurred on both dates; Isabel's handwritten name appears. Limitation: the sheet cannot be assigned to either session and does not show application completion, submission, or priority.\n2. Isabel Lindqvist portal history (portal record; April 8, 10:14 a.m.). Application is marked created and saved; no submitted status or timestamp showing staff receipt of a completed application is present. Limitation: absence of a portal event does not rule out every other delivery channel.\n3. Partial text export involving Isabel Lindqvist and Mariam Braithwaite (retained timestamps: April 8, 11:02 a.m.; April 8, 11:19 a.m.; April 12, 9:07 a.m.). Isabel asks \"did that go through?\"; Mariam says she can see only drafts until submission; Isabel says she sent everything earlier that week. Limitation: export skips the intervening four days and is not certified complete.\n4. Mariam Braithwaite recollection of calls (recalled dates: April 9 and April 11). Mariam says she repeated that the application remained a draft. Limitation: no contemporaneous call notes or recordings.\n5. Later applicant portal milestones (portal record; April 12-13). Submission at 8:42 a.m. April 12; screened April 12; accepted at 3:30 p.m. April 13. Limitation: no comparative qualification information is available.\n6. Operational scope and custody note (Clearwater Housing Trust; prepared for Xiomara Sheridan). This narrative is limited to reconstructing the supplied operational record. Fair-housing, legal, compliance, motive, and liability determinations are reserved to Eamon Kilgore; no complete case file is represented.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A readable, non-corrupt DOCX is submitted under the exact required filename.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"application_findings.docx","grader_hint":"Confirm that application_findings.docx exists at the submission root and opens successfully as a Word document."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The complete rendered document is no longer than three pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered application_findings.docx","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX using a standard office renderer and count all pages, including the evidence index."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document contains an identifiable findings narrative and an identifiable numbered evidence index.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Document headings and body","grader_hint":"Accept reasonable heading variants if the narrative and index are unmistakably separate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document is written for Xiomara Sheridan as the non-specialist owner representative rather than as an internal case note or legal brief.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Tone, framing, and terminology throughout","grader_hint":"Look for plain-language framing that equips Xiomara to understand the record without specialist portal or legal knowledge."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The opening gives a concise, neutral bottom-line finding rather than delaying the central conclusion until the evidence index.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening portion of the findings narrative","grader_hint":"The opening should state the calibrated result: the record shows creation and saving but not submission or staff receipt, while gaps prevent broader certainty."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The allegation is framed as two distinct propositions: failure to transmit Isabel Lindqvist's allegedly completed application and selection of a later applicant.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Issue statement","grader_hint":"Confirm that the document does not collapse the transmission allegation and later selection into a single proven event."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document expressly limits its scope to an operational reconstruction from the identified record.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope or introductory language","grader_hint":"Look for a clear description of the limited purpose and record basis, not merely a generic disclaimer."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The narrative identifies the material review period as April 6 through April 13.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Narrative chronology","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent wording that clearly brackets the first open house and acceptance date."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document reports both April 6 and April 13 open houses and connects the undated sign-in sheet only to the open-house process generally.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Narrative and sign-in-sheet index entry","grader_hint":"The sheet may not be assigned to one of the two dates."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document expressly states that Isabel's sign-in cannot establish which open house she attended.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Treatment of the undated sign-in sheet","grader_hint":"Credit only if the evidentiary limitation is stated, not merely implied by calling the sheet undated."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The portal event is accurately reported as application creation on April 8 at 10:14 a.m.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Portal chronology","grader_hint":"Check the date, time, and event type together."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The portal status is accurately described as saved but never submitted.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Portal finding","grader_hint":"The document must preserve the distinction between saved and submitted."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document states that the portal provides no timestamp showing staff receipt of a completed application.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Portal finding and limitations","grader_hint":"Do not credit language that converts the absence of a receipt timestamp into proof that receipt was impossible."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Isabel's April 8, 11:02 a.m. text asking whether the application went through is accurately identified.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Text chronology","grader_hint":"A faithful paraphrase is acceptable if the date, time, speaker, and uncertainty are retained."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Mariam's April 8, 11:19 a.m. response that she could see only drafts until submission is accurately identified.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Text chronology","grader_hint":"Confirm that the response is attributed to Mariam and does not claim she performed an additional search or action."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Isabel's April 12, 9:07 a.m. statement that she sent everything earlier that week is accurately identified as her statement.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Text chronology","grader_hint":"The wording must remain an attributed assertion rather than an independently verified submission event."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The narrative identifies the four-day gap between the retained April 8 and April 12 text messages as material.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Discussion of text-record limitations","grader_hint":"Look for an explanation that the gap limits reconstruction of intervening communications."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The partial text export is expressly described as not certified complete.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Text evidence description","grader_hint":"Equivalent language about unverified completeness is acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Mariam's recollection identifies calls on both April 9 and April 11.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Call-recollection discussion","grader_hint":"Both dates must be present."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recollected substance of both calls is accurately stated: Mariam says she repeated that the application remained a draft.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Call-recollection discussion","grader_hint":"The document must attribute this account to Mariam rather than present it as independently recorded fact."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The lack of contemporaneous call notes and recordings is expressly identified.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Call-evidence limitation","grader_hint":"Credit if both forms of missing corroboration are captured or if the language equivalently states that no contemporaneous record of the calls exists."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The later applicant's submission is accurately reported as April 12 at 8:42 a.m.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Later-application chronology","grader_hint":"Check the event type, date, and time."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The later applicant is accurately reported as screened on April 12.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Later-application chronology","grader_hint":"No unsupported screening outcome or criteria should be attached to this event."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The later applicant's acceptance is accurately reported as April 13 at 3:30 p.m.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Later-application chronology","grader_hint":"Check the date, time, and acceptance event."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document states that comparative qualification information is unavailable.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Limitations or comparative discussion","grader_hint":"The limitation must prevent any ranking of the applicants on qualifications."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Dated events are presented in chronological order without assigning an invented date to the sign-in sheet.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire findings chronology","grader_hint":"Verify sequence from April 6 through April 13 and confirm the undated item remains outside any falsely precise position."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document explains that created, saved, and submitted are different portal events with different evidentiary meanings.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Portal interpretation","grader_hint":"A mere list of labels is insufficient; the narrative should explain why the distinction affects the finding."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document states when the earliest-timestamp rule of thumb stops being reliable: when timestamps represent different event types rather than comparable submitted applications.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Application-order analysis","grader_hint":"Look for an explicit limitation on using Isabel's April 8 creation time to establish submission order."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The comparison between the two application records uses like-for-like milestones and does not compare Isabel's creation time directly with the later applicant's submission time as equivalent events.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparative chronology","grader_hint":"Credit if the document says only the later applicant has a recorded submission milestone."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document identifies April 12 as the material change point: the later application was submitted before Isabel's retained message claiming earlier transmission.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Period comparison","grader_hint":"The statement must preserve that Isabel's message is an assertion, not a verified portal event."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The principal affirmative finding is that the available portal record shows creation and saving but no recorded submission by Isabel.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Bottom line and findings","grader_hint":"This should appear as a supported record finding, not as a conclusion about why submission did not occur."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document states that the record does not verify Isabel's assertion that she completed and sent everything.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Finding on Isabel's assertion","grader_hint":"Use calibrated language such as 'does not verify' or 'does not establish,' not an accusation that the assertion was false."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document states that the record does not establish that Clearwater staff received and then failed to forward a completed application.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Finding on staff handling","grader_hint":"The absence of proof must not be phrased as categorical proof that no failure occurred."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document states that the record does not establish discriminatory selection, disparate treatment, or an improper preference for the later applicant.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Boundary of findings","grader_hint":"Accept comparable language that avoids deciding a fair-housing issue from the limited operational record."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not treat the portal status as complete exoneration because the text gap, undated sheet, and unrecorded calls leave unresolved factual gaps.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Overall conclusion and limitations","grader_hint":"Look for a balanced statement that the available record is insufficient for categorical exoneration."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Mariam's memory is treated as relevant but less independently verifiable than contemporaneous timestamped records.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source-weight discussion","grader_hint":"The document should neither discard the recollection nor elevate it to the status of a recording."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The retained texts are used as evidence of what the parties wrote at specific times, not as proof that the export captures the whole conversation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Treatment of text evidence","grader_hint":"Confirm that the narrative distinguishes message content from record completeness."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The sign-in sheet is used only to support possible open-house contact, not application completion, submission, or priority.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Treatment of sign-in evidence","grader_hint":"Credit if the document confines the sheet to its proper evidentiary scope."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The analysis distinguishes absence of a recorded event from proof that the event could not have occurred through any channel.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reasoning about missing records","grader_hint":"Look for explicit caution about negative evidence; the document may still state what the portal itself does not record."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The possibility of a fair-housing issue is acknowledged without making a legal or regulatory determination.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope boundary or conclusion","grader_hint":"The document should recognize the significance of the complaint while staying within an operational fact-finding role."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Eamon Kilgore is identified as the appropriate person for fair-housing or legal determinations.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Boundary or escalation language","grader_hint":"Accept language that clearly reserves legal characterization to Eamon without asking him to determine operational facts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Operational findings are clearly separated from questions of legal liability, discrimination, or compliance.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Structure and conclusion","grader_hint":"The boundary should be understandable to Xiomara and not buried in fine-print disclaimer language."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document makes no inference about Isabel's protected-class status.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire document","grader_hint":"Credit only if no protected characteristic is stated, guessed, or implied as fact."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document makes no unsupported inference about the motive of Mariam, Clearwater, Latchford Media, Xiomara, or the later applicant.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire document","grader_hint":"Distinguish neutral descriptions of actions from claims of intent, favoritism, deception, or bad faith."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not assert that the portal malfunctioned.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Portal discussion","grader_hint":"It may state that the available record cannot determine why submission was not recorded, but it may not diagnose a malfunction."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not assert that messages, records, or application materials were deleted.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Discussion of missing material","grader_hint":"Calling an export partial or incomplete is permissible; claiming deletion without evidence is not."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not characterize the identified materials as a complete case file.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope and evidence descriptions","grader_hint":"Look for affirmative recognition that the reconstruction is based on a limited record."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not claim that the later applicant displaced Isabel or caused her not to receive the unit.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparative analysis","grader_hint":"Temporal sequence alone must not be converted into displacement or causation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not claim Isabel had application priority merely because her portal record was created earlier.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Application-order analysis","grader_hint":"The finding should hinge on comparable submitted milestones, not account or draft creation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The bottom-line finding is materially consistent wherever it appears in the opening, narrative, and conclusion.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening, body, and conclusion","grader_hint":"No section should shift from 'not established' to categorical fault, exoneration, submission, or non-submission beyond what the record supports."},{"rubric_item_id":"R51","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each material factual sentence in the narrative contains or immediately shares a clear citation to one or more numbered evidence entries.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Narrative citations and evidence index","grader_hint":"Sample every paragraph and verify that externally checkable facts map to index numbers; analytical and scope statements need not be cited as facts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R52","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Inferences and evaluative conclusions are visibly distinguished from direct observations or attributed recollections.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Wording throughout the narrative","grader_hint":"Look for calibrated terms such as records, states, recalls, supports, does not establish, and cannot determine."},{"rubric_item_id":"R53","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The narrative squarely identifies the tension between Isabel's April 12 assertion and the portal's lack of a submission event without declaring either source false.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reconciliation of text and portal evidence","grader_hint":"Both pieces must be presented together and the unresolved conflict must remain explicit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R54","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Evidence-index entries use a unique, continuous numbering scheme that is also used by the narrative citations.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence index and narrative","grader_hint":"Confirm that numbers are not duplicated or skipped without explanation and that citations use the same identifiers."},{"rubric_item_id":"R55","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The evidence index accounts for the open-house sign-in record, Isabel's portal history, the partial text export, Mariam's call recollection, and the later applicant's portal milestones.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Numbered evidence index","grader_hint":"These may be five entries or sensibly divided into more entries, but every evidence category must be represented."},{"rubric_item_id":"R56","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Each evidence-index entry identifies the source or custodian, the relevant date or undated status, the pertinent content, and any material limitation.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Numbered evidence index","grader_hint":"Apply the fields contextually; for example, a recollection has recalled dates and no recording, while the sign-in sheet is expressly undated."},{"rubric_item_id":"R57","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every citation in the narrative resolves to an existing evidence-index entry whose description supports the associated statement.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Narrative citations and evidence index","grader_hint":"Check both referential integrity and substantive fit; a citation number that exists but concerns a different source does not pass."},{"rubric_item_id":"R58","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document uses only the minimum personal information needed to distinguish the applicant, staff member, owner representative, and later applicant record.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire document","grader_hint":"No unnecessary contact details, demographic details, account identifiers, or invented personal information should appear."},{"rubric_item_id":"R59","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document makes clear which propositions Xiomara can safely describe as record findings and which allegations remain unverified.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Bottom line and concluding synthesis","grader_hint":"A non-specialist owner representative should be able to distinguish supportable facts from claims that should not be repeated as established."},{"rubric_item_id":"R60","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The narrative is neutral and avoids advocacy language that reads as spin for either Clearwater or Isabel.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Tone throughout","grader_hint":"Watch for loaded terms such as fabricated, negligent, obviously, cleared, vindicated, or proven discriminatory where the record does not support them."},{"rubric_item_id":"R61","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Portal terminology is used consistently and precisely throughout the document.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire document","grader_hint":"Created, saved, submitted, received, screened, and accepted must not be used interchangeably."},{"rubric_item_id":"R62","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"No factual content beyond the stated record is presented as known.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire document","grader_hint":"Check especially for invented communications, portal actions, qualification details, property policies, reasons for selection, and identities or characteristics of the later applicant."},{"rubric_item_id":"R63","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"All stated dates and times agree with the corresponding evidence-index entries and remain consistent across the document.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Narrative and evidence index","grader_hint":"Cross-check April 8 at 10:14, 11:02, and 11:19; April 12 at 8:42 and 9:07; and April 13 at 3:30, along with the dated open houses and recalled calls."},{"rubric_item_id":"R64","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Uncertainty is expressed specifically by naming the missing or limited evidence rather than through vague boilerplate.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Limitations and conclusion","grader_hint":"Look for concrete links to the undated sheet, four-day text gap, uncertified export, absent portal receipt event, unrecorded calls, and missing qualification comparison."},{"rubric_item_id":"R65","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"As a whole, the document gives Xiomara a coherent and defensible account she can use without asking the author to resolve contradictions, define portal events, or identify the legal boundary.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Complete rendered document","grader_hint":"Judge professional usability, synthesis, readability, and whether the calibrated conclusion follows from the indexed evidence."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Clearwater Housing Trust must give a property owner a defensible operational account of a disputed application sequence before the owner responds to the applicant. The record supports some timing findings but contains material gaps and does not support a fair-housing or liability determination.","difficulty_sources":["Distinguishing portal creation and saving from submission and receipt","Reconciling timestamped records with an incomplete text export and uncorroborated recollection","Limiting a common earliest-timestamp shortcut to comparable process events","Separating operational findings from fair-housing and legal determinations","Maintaining sentence-level evidence traceability within a three-page limit"],"authoring_plan":{"solver_instance":"The solver acts as Iris Macaulay, a senior real estate sales agent preparing an owner-facing operational findings narrative before an applicant complaint is answered.","intended_verdict":"The available record supports that Isabel created and saved a portal application but does not show a submitted application or staff receipt of a completed application. It therefore does not establish her transmission assertion or a staff failure to forward a completed application. The incomplete communications record prevents categorical exoneration, and the record cannot resolve comparative qualifications, motive, discrimination, liability, or causation.","fixed_record":{"property_context":"Clearwater Housing Trust manages leasing for Latchford Media's 44-unit building.","allegation":"Isabel Lindqvist alleges that her completed application was not sent to the owner and that a later applicant received the unit.","open_house_record":"Open houses occurred April 6 and April 13. An undated sign-in sheet includes Isabel's handwritten name but cannot be assigned to either session.","isabel_portal_record":"The application was created April 8 at 10:14 a.m. and saved, but it never reached submitted status. There is no portal timestamp showing staff receipt of a completed application.","text_record":"The partial export contains Isabel's April 8 11:02 a.m. question, Mariam's April 8 11:19 a.m. draft-status response, and Isabel's April 12 9:07 a.m. assertion that she sent everything earlier in the week. The intervening four days are absent and completeness is not certified.","call_recollection":"Mariam recalls April 9 and April 11 calls in which she repeated that the application remained a draft. No call notes or recordings corroborate the recollection.","later_application_record":"The later applicant submitted April 12 at 8:42 a.m., was screened that day, and was accepted April 13 at 3:30 p.m.","comparative_record":"No comparative qualification information is available."},"professional_rules_to_apply":["Distinguish direct records, attributed statements, recollections, inferences, and unresolved allegations.","Treat created, saved, submitted, received, screened, and accepted as distinct events.","Compare order only using equivalent process milestones; an earlier creation timestamp does not establish priority over a later submitted application.","Use contemporaneous timestamped records for what they directly show, while recognizing that missing records do not prove an event was impossible.","Treat an undated sign-in sheet as evidence of possible contact only, not as proof of attendance on a particular date or application submission.","Treat a partial, uncertified text export as evidence of retained messages but not as a complete conversation.","Treat unrecorded staff recollection as relevant attributed evidence, not as a contemporaneous record.","Do not infer qualification ranking where comparative qualification information is absent.","Do not infer motive, protected status, disparate treatment, portal malfunction, deletion, displacement, or causation from timing alone.","Separate operational fact-finding from fair-housing, liability, and legal determinations reserved to Eamon Kilgore.","State both sides of each doctrinal limit: what the record supports and the broader claim it does not support.","Ensure each material factual sentence maps to a numbered evidence-index entry."],"rule_of_thumb_tension":{"common_practice":"The team often uses the earliest portal timestamp to describe application order.","failure_condition":"That shortcut is not valid when the compared timestamps represent different event types. Isabel's April 8 event is creation, while the later applicant's April 12 event is submission.","required_document_effect":"The narrative must explain the limit and must not use Isabel's creation time to establish submission priority."},"functional_boundary":{"within_scope":"Reconstruct the operational record, describe source limitations, and identify supported and unsupported factual propositions.","outside_scope":"Determine discrimination, fair-housing compliance, motive, liability, or legal sufficiency.","boundary_owner":"Eamon Kilgore handles fair-housing and legal determinations."},"evidence_index_contract":{"required_vocabulary":["numbered evidence index","created","saved","submitted","screened","accepted"],"minimum_evidence_categories":["open-house sign-in record","Isabel portal history","partial text export","Mariam call recollection","later applicant portal milestones"],"entry_information":"Each entry should identify the source or custodian, relevant date or undated status, pertinent content, and material limitation.","citation_relationship":"Narrative citations must use the same unique index numbers and each citation must substantively support its associated factual statement."},"space_feasibility":"A concise findings narrative of roughly 700 to 900 words plus five to seven compact evidence-index entries can fit within three professionally formatted pages. The rubric does not require reproducing texts at length or adding a separate legal analysis.","offline_feasibility_check":"A reference DOCX can be authored and rendered offline using Python office libraries or LibreOffice. All fixed facts, required names, timestamps, conclusions, terminology, and scope boundaries are present in the request or derive from standard real-estate evidence-handling judgment. No external law, current market information, or internet lookup is required."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"primary_plus_appendix","structure":"supplied_template"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"findings_document","filename":"application_findings.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"Owner-facing findings narrative concerning the disputed application sequence, followed by a numbered evidence index.","required":true,"constraints":["Use exactly the filename application_findings.docx.","Place the file at the top level of the working directory.","Limit the complete document to three pages.","Include a neutral findings narrative and a numbered evidence index.","Make factual statements traceable to the evidence index.","Do not invent missing evidence, comparative qualifications, motives, or legal conclusions."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"communicate_stakeholders","work_product":"sales_proposal","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"professional_judgment"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"real_estate_sales_agents","sector":"real_estate_rental_leasing","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":2.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"domain_expert","reviewer_policy":"A real-estate operations reviewer should verify the chronology, portal-event distinctions, source limitations, and owner usability. A second reviewer familiar with fair-housing issue spotting should confirm that the document recognizes the legal significance without making unsupported legal, motive, or protected-class findings.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No underlying exhibits are supplied; the fixed record facts are embedded in the workplace request.","The work product is an operational findings narrative, not a legal opinion or final response to the applicant.","Rendering can vary slightly by office suite, so the page cap must be checked using a standard office renderer."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:05:16+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:05:16+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:05:16+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:05:16+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R11', 'R13', 'R20']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:05:16+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/2bd4c847a4cfb895","declared_deliverables":["application_findings.docx"]};
